#op: develop
A lens of the tip connects it to its parent, the newest version under
`history/`, and names the parent's instance after that version. Here the
`ForwardLens` was written when the newest version was 1.0, and then 1.1 was
cut beneath it, as happens when the tip's branch is rebased onto one that cut
a version. The lens still names `v1_0`, so it no longer connects the tip to its
parent. Renaming the parameter is not enough on its own: the mappings were
written against 1.0's schema, and need review against 1.1's.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
	b: int
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		b: 0
	}
}
-- ship/history/1.1.thema --
Schema: {
	a:  string
	b:  int
	c?: string
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
	b: int
	d: bool
}

ForwardLens: {
	v1_0: _
	tip: {
		d: false
	}
}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0150",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "ForwardLens in tip.thema names v1_0, but the tip's parent is 1.1",
      "primary": {
        "file": "ship/tip.thema",
        "line": 8,
        "col": 2,
        "offset": 57,
        "origin": "user"
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "label": "the lens was written against an older parent, 1.0; the newest version under history/ is now 1.1, history/1.1.thema"
        }
      ],
      "help": [
        "declare v1_1: _ in place of v1_0, and review the mappings against 1.1's schema"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "errors": 1,
    "warnings": 0,
    "notes": 0
  }
}
